From 4f01a52bfed9d0a7e0b02e37d93cb7f05e987c91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:52:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strings: the help of the Dolby Vision for the menus setting
 tells about the confirmation

The help of videoscreen.hadesdvmenus (#40991 in the core, #32191 in Estuary, in English
and Spanish) was rewritten by the plain-language pass of the settings before the
confirmation question of the setting (#40992 / #32196) existed. It now says that turning
the setting on asks the user to confirm the picture, and that without a Yes within 15
seconds it goes back to Off by itself.

Found while putting two changes together.
---
 addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po           | 2 +-
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po  | 2 +-
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po  | 4 ++--
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po  | 4 ++--
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po  | 4 ++--
 5 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index 20309fc..7b65d2e 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -26947,7 +26947,7 @@ msgstr ""
 #. Hades: help of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvmenus"
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#40991"
-msgid "Keeps the TV in Dolby Vision while the menus are on screen, so a Dolby Vision video starts, and goes back to the menus, without the TV switching its picture mode. Any other video (SDR, HDR10, HDR10+, HLG) makes the TV switch once more at its start and once more at its end. The menus are sent at a fixed brightness (the white of 'GUI and subtitle brightness in HDR') and the TV shows them in its Dolby Vision picture mode, which may look different from its SDR one. While the menus change, the graphics chip converts each frame. Shown only for a TV that takes Dolby Vision, with the menus at 3840x2160. If the TV shows a black or broken picture, turn this off. Off by default."
+msgid "Keeps the TV in Dolby Vision while the menus are on screen, so a Dolby Vision video starts, and goes back to the menus, without the TV switching its picture mode. Any other video (SDR, HDR10, HDR10+, HLG) makes the TV switch once more at its start and once more at its end. The menus are sent at a fixed brightness (the white of 'GUI and subtitle brightness in HDR') and the TV shows them in its Dolby Vision picture mode, which may look different from its SDR one. While the menus change, the graphics chip converts each frame. Shown only for a TV that takes Dolby Vision, with the menus at 3840x2160. When you turn it on, a question asks you to confirm that the picture is right; unless you answer Yes within 15 seconds it goes back to Off by itself, so a black picture needs no remote to get out of it. Off by default."
 msgstr ""
 
 #. Hades: text of the question that follows turning on "videoscreen.hadesdvmenus"; translated in Estuary (#32196). {0}: seconds
